1.1.text:
Article 6

(1) Protection of Women and Children is the obligation and responsibility of the Regional Government, community, parents and family;

(2) The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in article 6 paragraph (1) include:

a. implementing policies for the protection of women and children from acts of violence established by the government;
b. establishing policies, programs and activities for the protection of women and children from acts of violence;
c. cooperating in the implementation of Women and Children from acts of violence;
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure in the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence; e. allocating budgets for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
f. allocating budgets for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence according to regional financial capacity and;
g. fostering and supervising the implementation of Protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(3) To anticipate the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children, the Regional Government is obliged to provide and organize services in the form of:
a. establishing and facilitating the operation of integrated service institutions for victims by involving relevant community elements;
b. encouraging community awareness of the importance of protection for victims.

Article 7

The obligations and responsibilities of the community as referred to in Article 6 paragraph (1) include:

a. preventing acts of violence against women and children; b. providing protection to victims;
c. providing emergency assistance;
d. providing information and/or reporting acts of violence against women and children to the competent authorities; and e. participating in the handling of victims of violence.

Article 8

The obligations of parents and/or family as referred to in Article 6 paragraph (1) include:

a. preventing all forms of violence and protecting women and children as family members;
b. providing support for women and children victims of violence who are part of family members;

Article 17

(1) The Regional Government is obligated to conduct guidance on the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence. (2) Guidance as referred to in paragraph (1), includes: a. guidelines and fulfillment standards;

b. technical guidance and training;

c. provision of facilities; and

d. monitoring and evaluation.

CHAPTER II

RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE Article 5

Victims have the right to receive:

a. respect for dignity and worth as human beings; b. protection from family, community and regional government;
c. information;
d. optimal service;
e. continuous service up to the rehabilitation stage; f. confidential handling;
g. psychological assistance and legal aid; and
h. self-determination;

Article 1

Implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence is carried out based on Pancasila, the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia, as well as the principles and basic rights as regulated in the convention on women and children which include:

a. Respect for human rights;
b. Non-discrimination;
c. The best interests of women and or children; d. The right to life, survival, and development; e. Respect for the opinions of women and children; f. Justice and gender equality; and
g. Protection of victims.

Article 3

The prevention activities of the occurrence of violence as referred to in article 3 include:

a. Socialization;
b. Dissemination; and
c. Training;

